# Runtime configuration
#
# A derived repository keeps this file — bootstrap names `.gitignore` as one of the
# generic files that survives the vendor step — and both bootstrap and the sangha
# protocol prescribe `git add -A`. One was found carrying an untracked `.env` that
# any of those would have staged. It had never been committed; the next one may not
# be so lucky.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Agent worktrees. `.claude/worktrees/<name>` is a git worktree — an embedded
# repository — and `git add -A` stages it as a gitlink pointing at a commit no
# clone can resolve. Same family as the `.env` above: a directory that appears
# in a working tree without anyone putting it there, in a repository whose
# protocols prescribe `git add -A`.
.claude/worktrees/

# Rust
# The yidam binary, installed per-repository rather than into ~/.cargo/bin so that
# a machine with several yidam repositories does not run one repo's pinned build
# against another's corpus. `.yidam/bin` in a derived repo, `.local/bin` here.
.local/
.yidam/bin/

# Artifacts `yidam vault materialize` hardlinks out of the machine-wide cache so a
# person or a connector has a real file with a real name. `materialize` refuses to
# write until this entry exists.
.yidam/vault/
target/
# `cargo --target-dir` output under any name. `target/` alone missed `target-pin/`, which a
# `git add -A` then swept 567 build artifacts out of.
target-*/

# Python
__pycache__/
# fastembed downloads its ONNX weights to a cwd-relative directory the first time a model is
# resolved, so `yidam index-build` run from a repository root leaves 23MB of untracked model
# blobs in it. Not a build artifact of this repository, and not one of a derived repository
# either — `bootstrap.md` keeps this file when a repo is derived, so the rule travels.
.fastembed_cache/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Node / TypeScript
node_modules/
dist/
.pnpm-store/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Captured agent transcripts under a committed baseline.
#
# The baseline itself is committed — the corpus, the history, and the verdicts — because it
# is a golden fixture the checks are re-run against. The raw event stream is not: it runs to
# a couple of megabytes per run, and roughly three quarters of that is tool results echoing
# prelude files this repository already contains. Everything the harness or its tests read
# from it — the resolved model, turns, duration, cost, permission denials, turns before the
# first write — is parsed once and persisted into `structural.json`, so the baseline stays
# self-describing without carrying the stream.
#
# Ignored rather than deleted, so `harness run` still writes one and it is there to read
# while a result is being investigated.
yidam/tests/results/**/transcript.jsonl

# LanceDB
*.lance/

# LEAN / Lake
# `lake build` writes .olean/.ilean/.c into `.lake/` beside the sources it compiles. The
# manifest is committed — it is the dependency pin, and this package has zero dependencies,
# which is a fact worth being able to see change.
yidam/prelude/sdks/spec/.lake/

# mise
.mise.local.toml

# macOS
.DS_Store
